ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":89,"prev":91,"next":93,"titles":95,"firmware":264},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":10,"order":11,"path":12,"context":13,"summary":19,"status":20,"firmware":21,"facts":28,"procedures":58,"parameters":65,"related":66,"body":69,"sources":70,"official_url":32,"controls":77},"sequencer.track-scale","Track scale",[5,6,7,8,9],"step resolution","time division","track speed","half speed","double speed","sequencer",62,"knowledge/manual/units/sequencer/track-scale.md",{"modes":14,"screens":17},[15,16],"instrument","auxiliary",[18],"bar","`bar + accidental` sets how long one step of the selected track lasts: at 1 a sixteenth note, at 4 a quarter note, at 1/2 a thirty-second. Each track has its own scale.","outdated-in-guide",{"min":22,"changed_in":23,"guide_version":26,"verified_on":27},"1.0.9",[24,25],"1.0.15","1.1.25","1.1.15",null,[29,34,38,41,44,47,50,54],{"id":30,"text":31,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"set","Holding `bar` and pressing a black key sets the track scale, the time one step takes; every track keeps its own.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/sequencer#extend-with-bar","official",{"id":35,"text":36,"source":37,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"meaning","The scale multiplies the length of every step; at 4 a step lasts four normal steps, so four steps fill a 4/4 bar.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/get-started#4.3%20adding-chords",{"id":39,"text":40,"source":37,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"four","`bar + accidental 4`, the black key marked 4, sets scale 4; the step lights then move four times slower.",{"id":42,"text":43,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"double","Scale 1/2 halves every step, so a pattern plays at double time beside tracks at 1; scale 2 doubles every step, half time. A pattern at 1/2 lasts half as long, so it plays twice in a scene of its length at 1.",{"id":45,"text":46,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"longer","Raising the scale is how a pattern outgrows four bars; 64 steps at scale 16 last 64 bars.",{"id":48,"text":49,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"guide-list","TE's guide lists the scales 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 16 and 1/2.",{"id":51,"text":52,"source":53,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"fractions","The changelog also names 1/5 and 1/7, repaired in OS 1.0.15.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.0.15",{"id":55,"text":56,"source":57,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"odd-scales","OS 1.1.25 gave the odd scales 3, 5, 6 and 7 their own quantisation grid, so 5 and 7 exist too.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.1.25",[59],{"id":30,"goal":60,"preconditions":61,"steps":62,"result":27,"source":32,"firmware_min":27,"verified_on":27,"confidence":33},"Change how long each step of the track lasts",[],[63],{"keys":64,"note":27,"set":27},"bar + accidental",[],[67,68],"sequencer.bar-menu","sequencer.bars-and-length","Tracks at different scales share a scene: a slow pad at 4 next to hi-hats at 1/2. TE ties only the\nkey marked 4 to a value; which keys give 16 and the fractions is not documented.",[71,73,74,76],{"url":32,"kind":72},"guide",{"url":37,"kind":72},{"url":53,"kind":75},"changelog",{"url":57,"kind":75},[78,79,80,81,82,83,84,85,86,87,88],"key.bar","keyboard.fs3","keyboard.gs3","keyboard.as3","keyboard.cs4","keyboard.ds4","keyboard.fs4","keyboard.gs4","keyboard.as4","keyboard.cs5","keyboard.ds5",{"id":10,"title":90},"Sequencer",{"id":67,"title":92},"Bar menu",{"id":68,"title":94},"Bars and pattern length",{"basics.key-notation":96,"basics.main-modes":97,"basics.modules":98,"basics.track-buttons":99,"basics.linked-tracks":100,"basics.patterns-scenes-songs":101,"basics.workflow":102,"basics.firmware-versions":103,"hardware.layout":104,"hardware.power-and-charging":105,"hardware.connectors":106,"hardware.specifications":107,"hardwa